 "about": "Before the famous cliff dwellings, most people at Mesa Verde lived up on the mesa tops, and Far View was one of the busiest neighbourhoods: dozens of small villages farmed here between about 900 and 1300 CE. Mummy Lake, the big ring near the middle, was long called a reservoir; a 2014 study argued it was more likely an open-air plaza for gatherings, and the debate goes on. Mesa Verde is a national park and a World Heritage Site, and the Far View sites are a short walk from the main park road.",
